; Kempston joystick flag
;
; 0 = no joystick, 1 = a Kempston joystick is used in addition to the keys.
; Cleared and then set by #R$87CA if port $1F never returned bit 5 in 256 reads.
; Read by #R$96C9 (fire starts the game while the title tune plays) and by the
; movement code #R$8DD3, which then adds port $1F (right = bit 0, left = bit 1,
; fire = bit 4) to the key input. Observed: in the simulator, which returns 0
; for port $1F, the flag is 1 after the title screen; in the Bathroom snapshot
; with the flag poked to 1 the Kempston right input moves Willy right, with 0 it
; does not; fire at the tune starts the game.
@label=JoystickFlag
g$85CE DEFB $00
